  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The first term of an arithmetic series is ${a}_{1}=3$, the common difference is $d=6$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=243.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the number of terms, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d).\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${a}_{1}=3$, $d=6$ and ${S}_{N}=243$ into the above and solve for $N$, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 243 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 3+(N-1)\\cdot 6) \\\\ 243 & =\\frac{N}{2}(6+6N-6) \\\\ 243 & =\\frac{N}{2}(6N) \\\\ 243 & =3{N}^{2} \\\\ {N}^{2} & =81 \\\\ N & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative.",
